# CrossVi XTC/XTCH support contract

CrossVi reads a deliberately small, fixed-layout subset of the Xteink
XTC/XTCH formats. The contract is locked to real output from
[`bigbag/epub-to-xtc-converter`](https://github.com/bigbag/epub-to-xtc-converter),
commit `6792329e5ae77fac423db6b6cdc96af6afff82ae`.

## Supported subset

| Extension | Container | Page payload | Bit depth |
| --- | --- | --- | ---: |
| `.xtc` | `XTC` | `XTG` | 1-bit monochrome |
| `.xtch` | `XTCH` | `XTH` | 2-bit, four grayscale levels |

CrossVi accepts only:

- container version 1.0 (version bytes `1, 0`);
- uncompressed pages;
- portrait pages that are exactly 480 x 800 pixels;
- XTG pages in XTC and XTH pages in XTCH;
- bounded, terminated metadata and chapters whose page range is valid.

The byte-swapped version 0.1 is not accepted. No fixture produced by the
recommended converter was found that needs that compatibility exception.
Unsupported dimensions, compression, versions, mixed page types, truncated
payloads and inconsistent offsets/sizes fail closed.

## Page storage

XTG is row-major, MSB first. Each row occupies `(width + 7) / 8` bytes; bit 0
means black and bit 1 means white.

XTH stores two vertical bit planes. Each plane occupies
`width * ceil(height / 8)` bytes. Converter bit plane 0 is followed by bit
plane 1; together they select white, dark gray, light gray or black. All size
and offset arithmetic is checked before allocation or I/O.

The converter's page-table `size` includes the 22-byte XTG/XTH page header,
whereas the page-header `dataSize` describes payload bytes only. Chapter
offsets are 64-bit and converter chapter page numbers are 1-based.

## X3 and X4 display policy

- X4 portrait (480 x 800): native 1:1 pixels, without scaling.
- X3 portrait (528 x 792): aspect-preserving fit-to-screen, centered with
  letterboxing. The complete 480 x 800 source is visible; it is never cropped
  or stretched independently by axis.

Both XTC and XTCH use the same integer mapping and no second framebuffer.

## Reader features and limits

Metadata, chapter navigation, progress, reading statistics, cover/thumbnail
generation, recent books and sleep cover are supported. Reading time is
counted only after a page is displayed successfully; per-book start/finish
timestamps can be corrected from the statistics screen. Source identity is
streamed with bounded memory. Replacing a file at the same path quarantines the old path-keyed state
before the new book is opened; moving the same file uses the existing state
move transaction.

XTC/XTCH pages are pre-rendered images, not reflowable EPUB content. Font,
font-size and CSS changes, dictionary selection, clipping, KOReader position
sync and per-book typography settings therefore do not apply.

## Fixtures and validation status

The host fixtures and their provenance are in `test/xtc/resources/README.md`.
Synthetic malformed fixtures exercise parser bounds, and the converter XTC and
XTCH fixtures lock the real v1.0 byte contract. Host tests, sanitizers,
firmware builds and model-specific simulator checks do not constitute physical
device validation. X3/X4 hardware validation remains a release gate; see
`docs/contributing/hardware-validation.md`.

The historical gist linked by earlier versions remains useful background but
is not the source of truth when it differs from converter output:
<https://gist.github.com/CrazyCoder/b125f26d6987c0620058249f59f1327d>.
